  "summary": "home-gallery is a self-hosted photo/video gallery. A CLI tool indexes a source media directory into a FileIndex (+optional IndexJournal), extracts EXIF/preview/geo/AI meta into content-addressed StorageFile blobs, and builds a gzip JSON Entry database (id=sha1 of primary file) which it can rebuild, filter-rebuild, export to static/archive, and sync from a remote gallery via fetch. A web server serves read APIs over that Entry database (/api/database.json with substring search, /api/database/tree/:hash, /api/sources, /files) and a single-writer, append-only NDJSON UserActionEvent log (POST/GET /api/events) whose addTag/removeTag actions are applied in-memory to the entry tags; basic-auth/ip-whitelist gate the HTTP surface. It is an event-sourced, file-backed CRUD environment.",
